# Client-side routing.
#
# React Router owns every path below /. Without this, Cloudflare Pages looks
# for a file at /deals/abc123, does not find one, and returns its own 404 — so
# the app works when you click through it and breaks the moment anyone
# refreshes a page or opens a link you sent them. Buyers arrive on /pay/:id
# from an email, which is exactly that case.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the URL stays as the buyer sees it, and the router
# reads it.
/*    /index.html   200
